 ## Shared principles
-The core mechanism involves a periodic densification step, typically executed every 100 iterations, starting from iteration 100 up to the maximum iteration count [S2]. During this step, the algorithm evaluates each Gaussian $G_i$ based on two primary criteria: the accumulated view-space positional gradient magnitude $|\nabla_{\mathbf{p}} \mathcal{L}|_i$ and the spatial extent (scale/volume) of the Gaussian.
