 ## Subtopics
 
 ### [OTS+SAtn Densification](1488-ots-satn-densification.md)
-OTS+SAtn Densification is a density control strategy for 3D Gaussian Splatting designed to adapt principled splatting techniques (OTS+SAtn) to real-world scene reconstruction by aligning its hyperparameters with standard 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS). It solves the problem of uncontrolled primitive growth in large-scale scenes by imposing strict caps on the total number of Gaussians, ensuring that densification stops once a target count (e.g., 100k, 500k, 1m, or 5m) is reached. It differs from sibling methods by prioritizing parameter alignment with 3DGS to facilitate fair comparison and stability in real-world datasets, rather than introducing novel splitting heuristics.
