 ### [Steerable Densification with Sampling](3564-steerable-densification-with-sampling.md)
-Steerable Densification with Sampling is a density control method for 3D Gaussian Splatting that uses a score-based ranking of Gaussians to select candidates for resampling, guided by image loss and per-Gaussian attributes. It sets itself apart from standard 3DGS densification by incorporating explicit photometric loss and saliency metrics into the selection probability, executed at a significantly reduced frequency (every 500 iterations) to prevent the duplication of misplaced primitives.
