 ### [Soft Pruning](5590-soft-pruning.md)
-Soft Pruning is a density control method in 3D Gaussian Splatting that reduces the number of Gaussian primitives during the densification stage by removing those with low contribution to the training loss. It differs from its sibling [Hard Pruning](5591-hard-pruning.md) by occurring *during* the densification phase (specifically before opacity resets) rather than after, allowing the model to recover performance through subsequent refinement iterations. This approach maintains a robust Hessian approximation for optimization by eliminating Gaussians that have converged to low L1 loss.
